# DURABLE REPRO — `Option[<resource>].and_then` / `.flat_map` is a TYPE
# CONFUSION: `gg check` accepts, the C backend emits a SEGFAULTING binary, and
# the LLVM backend refuses to compile its own IR.
#
# Found while enumerating the siblings of the `.map()` receiver-emptying defect
# (Core #4, one fix all siblings). It is NOT the same bug: `.map()`/`.filter()`
# lose the write only for bare-param and field-access receivers and still run,
# whereas this one fails for a PLAIN LOCAL receiver too and is memory-unsafe.
#
# WRONG TODAY (measured at HEAD):
#   `gg check`  -> "OK: no semantic errors"          (accepts)
#   C backend   -> builds, binary exits **139 (SIGSEGV)**
#   LLVM backend-> **fails to compile**:
#                  llc: '%v28' defined with type 'i64' but expected 'ptr'
#                       %v60 = phi ptr [ %v28, %bb1 ], [ %v30, %bb2 ]
#
# That phi is the whole story: the two incoming edges disagree on whether the
# value is an integer or a pointer. LLVM's verifier catches the confusion; the
# C backend emits it silently and the result dereferences an integer as a
# pointer. The LLVM lane failing to build is therefore NOT a separate LLVM bug
# — it is the same defect, caught by a stricter instrument (Core #13: pick an
# instrument that can SEE the failure class).
#
# ⚠ RESOURCE-PAYLOAD-SPECIFIC. The identical program with an `int` payload
# (`Some(21).and_then((int x): Some(twice(x)))`) prints 42 and exits 0. So a
# fixture over a trivial payload is a FALSE NEGATIVE for this class — the
# payload must be a real heap resource, which is why `Money` wraps a BUILT
# `Vector[int]` rather than a literal.
#
# ⚠ `gg run` MASKS the C failure as exit 1 with no output (it does not
# propagate the child's signal status — filed separately). Build the binary and
# run it directly, or this looks like a build error.
#
# INTENDED (what this fixture asserts): both legs print their element count,
# `11` then `12`, and exit 0.
#
# ORACLE: ggdef is OUT OF SUBSET — "`.and_then()` is outside the phase-0
# subset". So this class has NO definitional adjudication (Core #9 note); the
# subset gap is filed with the `.map()` entry.

struct Money:
    Vector[int] cents

int size_of(Money m):
    return m.cents.len()

Vector[int] heap_cents(int n):
    Vector[int] c = Vector[int]()
    int i = 0
    while i < n:
        c.push(i)
        i = i + 1
    return c

Option[Money] make_opt(int n):
    return Some(Money(heap_cents(n)))

void main():
    Option[Money] a = make_opt(11)
    Option[int] ra = a.and_then((Money m): Some(size_of(m)))
    if ra is Some(v):
        print(v)

    Option[Money] b = make_opt(12)
    Option[int] rb = b.flat_map((Money m): Some(size_of(m)))
    if rb is Some(v):
        print(v)
